From 351472e66fc89b9b935f4aa86dbad37c1d8db01b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:24:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] tsbvm: host(name, args...) -- a way out for programs,
 chosen by the embedder

The VM had no files, network or environment. Add a Host trait the embedder
attaches (Vm::set_host); a program asks with host("fs.read", path). Arguments
go in as one JSON array and the answer comes out as one JSON value (json.rs),
the same carriage tsb_call uses. No host attached -> every host() is an error.

The command-line tsbvm attaches StdHost (not built for wasm32, so a drop
cannot carry it): env.get, fs.dirs/exists/read/write/mkdirp/copy/rmrf,
json.parse/stringify, exit, and with the `http` feature http.post_json
(ureq; off by default so the library stays free of a TLS stack).

exit is not an error the program can catch: a `try` around host("exit", n)
does not make it carry on (Vm::exit_code, checked before the handlers).
A 4xx/5xx from http.post_json is an answer ({status, body}), not a failure.

Tests (tests/host.rs) run the real binary on programs folded by tsubakic
(tests/fixtures/*.jl -> *.tsb). Checked with the catch-guard removed: the exit
test fails, so it is not vacuous.
